    "The installed context retains eleven candidates from fourteen points. Three unresolved high points remain visible as red markers without a fabricated robot pose.",
    "The partial low-mast context has six independent position candidates. The complete humanoid, both open hands and proposed wrist attachments remain visible; browser checks compare every actual mesh transform to its recorded pose.",
    "Both coil tie heads now face away from the wind arm. Temporary leg and brace ties keep full tails. Fixed prior hand/arm and hand/tail intersections remain reproducible negative witnesses.",
    "The complete original probe/wind sensor leads and both 0.5 m free network leads remain visible. Their original modular connectors sit on the actual tray floor. Final logger/splice/guy parts remain explicitly outside this partial inspection.",
    "The floor-tray candidate uses deep leg flexion and a raised unused arm. Additional views expose the active hand near the tray instead of relying on a rear-oblique image where the body occludes it.",
    "Source ground geometry gives a visible level datum and covers buried stakes. Its earth/soil appearance is authored; the scene does not validate soil bearing, anchoring or a standing controller."
  ],
